./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37975:If there are no values specified for the fo:text-align and style:justify-single-word 20.301 attributes within the same formatting properties element, the values of those attributes is set to start and false respectively.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37977:In the OpenDocument XSL-compatible namespace, the fo:text-align attribute does not support the inherit, inside, outside, or string values.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37979:The fo:text-align attribute is usable with the following elements: <style:list-level-properties> 17.19 and <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37981:The values of the fo:text-align attribute are start, end, left, right, center or justify.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37985:The fo:text-align attribute when used with the <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6 element specifies the alignment of text in a paragraph. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37989:The fo:text-align attribute is usable with the following element: <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37991:The values of the fo:text-align attribute are start, end, left, right, center or justify.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37995:The fo:text-align attribute when used with the <style:list-level-properties> 17.20 element specifies the alignment of list labels. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37997:If the text:list-level-position-and-space-mode 20.431 attribute on the same <style:list-level-properties> element has the value label-width-and-position, the fo:text-align attribute specifies the horizontal alignment of the list label within the width specified by the text:min-label-width 20.433 attribute. If the actual width of the list label is greater than the specified minimum width no alignment takes place.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37999:If the text:list-level-position-and-space-mode attribute on the same <style:list-level-properties> element has the value label-alignment, the value of the text:min-label-width attribute is treated as 0 and the fo:text-align attribute specifies the horizontal alignment of the list label at the alignment position. The alignment position is specified by the fo:margin-left 20.207 and fo:text-indent 20.225 attributes of its child element <style:list-level-label-alignment> 17.20.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38001:The defined values for the fo:text-align attribute are:
